== 4.5a syntactic linearity on the expression tree (conservative: anything unproven is nonlinear) ==
a*b              nonlinear  PASS
a+b-0.5          linear     PASS
a-2*b            linear     PASS
exp(a)-1         nonlinear  PASS
a^2              nonlinear  PASS
a*0+b            linear     PASS
abs(a)-b         nonlinear  PASS
(a-b)*(a+b)      nonlinear  PASS
2*(a+b)/3        linear     PASS
a/b              nonlinear  PASS
-a + 3           linear     PASS
exp(1)*a         linear     PASS
a*b - a*b + a    nonlinear  PASS
a^1              nonlinear  PASS
min(a, b)        nonlinear  PASS
1e3*a - b        linear     PASS
(a*b - a*b + a and a^1 are numerically linear; the syntactic rule calls them nonlinear on purpose: the cost is a warning and 5 starts, never a missed safeguard.)
A kink outside [-2, 2] that the old 3-point numeric check missed:  nonlinear 

== 4.5d warning rule: warn if any start is infeasible/failed OR spread > max(1e-6, 1e-6*|F_best|) ==
